Subject: IOCP: a widened AFD poll issued only once the old one's cancel completes
Why: On Windows a socket never has two AFD polls in flight: arm_events widened a poll (WRITE to READ|WRITE) by issuing the wider poll first and only then cancelling the narrower one, and on Windows 11 the wider one then never completed, so a runner whose send blocked as its receive queue emptied heard nothing more from its server and its QUIC connection idled out ten seconds after every connect (Jupiter, 2026-10-24). The poll for the union is now issued once the cancelled poll's completion is reclaimed, as wepoll and mio do; a refused issue wakes the socket's waiters to retry.

